# oracle: fix langevin omega yes with tally yes and zero yes on finite-size spheres of two types (scale 2 1.5), fix nve/sphere; the tally energy (f_2 and ecouple), erotate/sphere and the zeroed total force are compared every 5 steps over two runs (the tally energy restarts at the second run's first step)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
units           lj
atom_style      sphere
atom_modify     map array sort 0 0.0
lattice         sc 0.6
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
set             group all diameter 1.0 density 1.0
group           two id 2:27:3
set             group two type 2
set             group two diameter 0.8 density 1.5
velocity        all create 1.0 4928 loop all
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 0.2 0.8
pair_modify     table 0
timestep        0.002
fix             1 all nve/sphere
fix             2 all langevin 1.0 1.5 1.0 9182 omega yes tally yes zero yes scale 2 1.5
compute         er all erotate/sphere
variable        fx equal fcm(all,x)
thermo_style    custom step temp pe c_er f_2 ecouple econserve v_fx
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             20
run             15
